/id #edb/ref 17592186722822 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "019fc706-0b6f-5e71-bd93-48f390f5d96f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=10-0.5y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722798} {:answer/id #uuid "48163981-705f-543e-82ef-f43aa9af6abf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=280-7y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722802} {:answer/id #uuid "7536856c-4f4c-5a1f-8499-b126c8347103" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=100-2y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722812} {:answer/id #uuid "84b44ed0-512b-564b-85b5-9abe2bad163c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=3y^{2}-660" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722816} {:answer/id #uuid "e704c54c-ef4d-57cd-9327-51ec1b71ca42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=4y-280" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722829}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722812} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc47c207-1520-5bb5-be7b-24af88db01ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722823}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a32c437c-00e0-5c6d-bce2-be8b24bb7b39" :question/problem "Given that $y<50$ and $t\\ge 0$, which of the following is an inhibited growth equation throughout this range?" :question/worked-solution "An inhibited growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=k(a-y),\\qquad k>0.\n$$\n\nThe quantity must be below its equilibrium: $y<a$.\n\nThe matching choice is\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=100-2y.\n$$\n\n\n\nThe equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dt}&=280-7y \\\\ &=7(40-y) \\\\ a&=40\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dt}&=10-0.5y \\\\ &=0.5(20-y) \\\\ a&=20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dt}&=100-2y \\\\ &=2(50-y) \\\\ a&=50\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe choice $\\frac{dy}{dt}=280-7y$ has equilibrium $a=40<50$; the stated bound does *not* keep the quantity below this equilibrium throughout the allowed range.\n\nThe choice $\\frac{dy}{dt}=10-0.5y$ has equilibrium $a=20<50$; the stated bound does *not* keep the quantity below this equilibrium throughout the allowed range.\n\nThe choice $\\frac{dy}{dt}=3y^{2}-660$ is nonlinear in $y$; it is not the required constant-times-gap model.\n\nThe choice $\\frac{dy}{dt}=4y-280$ has a positive linear coefficient, so its rate is not a positive constant times the remaining gap.\n\nThe choice $\\frac{dy}{dt}=100-2y$ has $k=2>0$ and equilibrium $a=50$, consistent with $y<50$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722840 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "141c93f7-7168-54a3-a2a0-5cf46e3f7c11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=-5(y-40)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722834} {:answer/id #uuid "42b86b15-cea9-5bea-87e3-25fb3b1e1302" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=-5(y+40)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722837} {:answer/id #uuid "4d803104-6a52-58e1-ad52-7a5b09e25cca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=0.3(90-y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722839} {:answer/id #uuid "5751b010-1be8-5bc2-a968-7b7ef7c7a23f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=-5(40-y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722841} {:answer/id #uuid "94ee3255-e63a-5c19-8f0e-55af47672b16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=-0.3(90-y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722849}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722839} :answer-field/id #uuid "72ca5b10-5878-5a7a-a2d2-caaf232449c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722846}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "56f5c58a-09fc-5cbb-bd9d-806defddcfbf" :question/problem "Given that $y<90$ and $t\\ge 0$, which of the following is an inhibited growth equation throughout this range?" :question/worked-solution "An inhibited growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=k(a-y),\\qquad k>0.\n$$\n\nThe quantity must be below its equilibrium: $y<a$.\n\nThe matching choice is\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=0.3(90-y).\n$$\n\n\n\nThe equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dt}&=0.3(90-y) \\\\ a&=90\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dt}&=-5(y-40) \\\\ &=5(40-y) \\\\ a&=40\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dt}&=-5(y+40) \\\\ a&=-40\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe choice $\\frac{dy}{dt}=-5(40-y)$ has a positive linear coefficient, so its rate is not a positive constant times the remaining gap.\n\nThe choice $\\frac{dy}{dt}=0.3(90-y)$ has $k=0.3>0$ and equilibrium $a=90$, consistent with $y<90$.\n\nThe choice $\\frac{dy}{dt}=-0.3(90-y)$ has a positive linear coefficient, so its rate is not a positive constant times the remaining gap.\n\nThe choice $\\frac{dy}{dt}=-5(y-40)$ has equilibrium $a=40<90$; the stated bound does *not* keep the quantity below this equilibrium throughout the allowed range.\n\nThe choice $\\frac{dy}{dt}=-5(y+40)$ has equilibrium $a=-40<90$; the stated bound does *not* keep the quantity below this equilibrium throughout the allowed range."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722848 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26e624c7-c1ae-56d4-9f83-626220fb748c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=-10(y+60)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722836} {:answer/id #uuid "6593768c-1233-5271-84c8-1cfd0fc7149e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=-10(y-20)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722844} {:answer/id #uuid "6fc901d5-1451-55a8-967e-435a9e496c05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=10(y-20)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722845} {:answer/id #uuid "96837ecf-f7ef-5cfe-a072-fd2dfe8425d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=0.5(60-y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722850} {:answer/id #uuid "ec887599-e142-5f7e-91b2-c04ea0904849" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=0.5(y-60)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722853}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722850} :answer-field/id #uuid "771e3848-303e-558c-8384-d0facc0a7e0a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722847}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8c8fe26e-af99-5504-8574-95df30bc1d62" :question/problem "Given that $y<60$ and $t\\ge 0$, which of the following is an inhibited growth equation throughout this range?" :question/worked-solution "An inhibited growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=k(a-y),\\qquad k>0.\n$$\n\nThe quantity must be below its equilibrium: $y<a$.\n\nThe matching choice is\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=0.5(60-y).\n$$\n\n\n\nThe equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dt}&=-10(y-20) \\\\ &=10(20-y) \\\\ a&=20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dt}&=0.5(60-y) \\\\ a&=60\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dt}&=-10(y+60) \\\\ a&=-60\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe choice $\\frac{dy}{dt}=10(y-20)$ has a positive linear coefficient, so its rate is not a positive constant times the remaining gap.\n\nThe choice $\\frac{dy}{dt}=-10(y-20)$ has equilibrium $a=20<60$; the stated bound does *not* keep the quantity below this equilibrium throughout the allowed range.\n\nThe choice $\\frac{dy}{dt}=0.5(60-y)$ has $k=0.5>0$ and equilibrium $a=60$, consistent with $y<60$.\n\nThe choice $\\frac{dy}{dt}=-10(y+60)$ has equilibrium $a=-60<60$; the stated bound does *not* keep the quantity below this equilibrium throughout the allowed range.\n\nThe choice $\\frac{dy}{dt}=0.5(y-60)$ has a positive linear coefficient, so its rate is not a positive constant times the remaining gap."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722852 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01b6b7c0-887e-5eea-8567-ebfe8160d0fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=-4(90-y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722833} {:answer/id #uuid "259a6af3-ad82-5793-b0d7-bfe642a9eadc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=-5(y-20)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722835} {:answer/id #uuid "432db498-e7d0-5a5f-aa52-951ad3f2adeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=-5(y+90)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722838} {:answer/id #uuid "5fd9378c-d677-5cc9-9869-8db4bc266aec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=5(y-20)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722843} {:answer/id #uuid "988775db-50a9-59fc-a0bd-dba5e29b1a7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=4(90-y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722851}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186722851} :answer-field/id #uuid "59486abb-027f-58a1-8def-a50c867baa2c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186722842}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d8a65b99-ba87-5c6e-9d84-63184e61e54e" :question/problem "Given that $y<90$ and $t\\ge 0$, which of the following is an inhibited growth equation throughout this range?" :question/worked-solution "An inhibited growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=k(a-y),\\qquad k>0.\n$$\n\nThe quantity must be below its equilibrium: $y<a$.\n\nThe matching choice is\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=4(90-y).\n$$\n\n\n\nThe equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dt}&=-5(y-20) \\\\ &=5(20-y) \\\\ a&=20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dt}&=-5(y+90) \\\\ a&=-90\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dt}&=4(90-y) \\\\ a&=90\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe choice $\\frac{dy}{dt}=-5(y-20)$ has equilibrium $a=20<90$; the stated bound does *not* keep the quantity below this equilibrium throughout the allowed range.\n\nThe choice $\\frac{dy}{dt}=5(y-20)$ has a positive linear coefficient, so its rate is not a positive constant times the remaining gap.\n\nThe choice $\\frac{dy}{dt}=-5(y+90)$ has equilibrium $a=-90<90$; the stated bound does *not* keep the quantity below this equilibrium throughout the allowed range.\n\nThe choice $\\frac{dy}{dt}=-4(90-y)$ has a positive linear coefficient, so its rate is not a positive constant times the remaining gap.\n\nThe choice $\\frac{dy}{dt}=4(90-y)$ has $k=4>0$ and equilibrium $a=90$, consistent with $y<90$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186723039 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "759b643d-751d-5b17-9b4d-9ce9fb6ce046" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$14$ days" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723043} {:answer/id #uuid "765c5c67-942d-5b5d-83c4-979cdb2900bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$10$ days" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723044} {:answer/id #uuid "8865500f-8be2-5bcb-8bc9-9c2b54aa9a0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$54$ days" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723047} {:answer/id #uuid "afb16777-a750-5cbe-9244-607ed3a733c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$7$ days" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723049} {:answer/id #uuid "b1fb036a-c6e0-5fe4-8cfc-274430d6f58c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$27$ days" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723050}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186723050} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe0bd758-de5c-5de1-97d1-611934d6f888" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723065}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "412bf08c-c57d-591f-af85-b5b243efa8bf" :question/problem "The number of students affected by flu $P(t)$ increases toward a maximum of $1000$ students. Time $t\\ge 0$ is measured in days from the start of monitoring. At $t=0$, the quantity is $470$ students. At $t=12$, it is $770$ students. At what time $t$, measured from the start of monitoring, does the quantity reach $920$ students? Round to the nearest integer.\n\n*Hint: Assume an inhibited growth model.*" :question/worked-solution "The growth rate is proportional to the remaining deficit. Thus\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=k(1000-P).\n$$\n\nSeparate and integrate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dP}{1000-P}&=k\\,dt \\\\ -\\ln|1000-P|&=kt+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe deficit is positive on this growth branch. Exponentiating and setting $K=e^{-C}>0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1000-P&=e^{-kt-C} \\\\ &=Ke^{-kt} \\\\ P(t)&=1000-Ke^{-kt}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the initial condition:\n\n$$\nK=1000-470=530.\n$$\n\nCalibrate the rate with the later observation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}530e^{-12k}&=230 \\\\ -12k&=\\ln\\left(\\frac{23}{53}\\right) \\\\ k&=\\frac{1}{12}\\ln\\left(\\frac{53}{23}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$\nP(t)=1000-530e^{-kt}.\n$$\n\nFor the requested target, solve for the original time $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}80&=530e^{-k(t-0)} \\\\ -k(t-0)&=\\ln\\left(\\frac{8}{53}\\right) \\\\ t&=0+\\frac{\\ln\\left(\\frac{53}{8}\\right)}{k} \\\\ &\\approx 27.180483 \\\\ &\\approx 27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is approximately $27$ days from the start of monitoring."}]}
